## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation:**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1` package using pnpm (the project's package manager)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` to lock the dependency versions

**2. Analytics Configuration:**
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate the Analytics component
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout

### Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) following Next.js App Router best practices. The component is placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it doesn't interfere with the existing page structure and accessibility features.

The implementation preserves:
- All existing imports and font configurations
- The skip-to-content accessibility link
- The original HTML structure and styling
- All metadata and SEO settings

### Testing Results

✅ **Linting:** Passed without errors  
✅ **Build:** Completed successfully - all 13 routes generated  
✅ **Type Safety:** The Analytics component integrates properly with TypeScript

### Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard by navigating to Analytics in the sidebar and clicking the Enable button
2. Deploy the project to Vercel - the Analytics tracking will activate automatically after deployment
3. After deployment, visitor and page view data will be collected and visible in the Vercel dashboard

The tracking script will make requests to a unique analytics endpoint visible in the browser's Network tab.
